From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Varun Gupta <varun.gupta@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 16:39:46 +0530
Subject: drm/pagemap: guard migrate_vma fault_page initializer on older kernels

Older kernels (e.g. 5.15) have a smaller struct migrate_vma layout and do not
provide .fault_page or newer migrate flags used by upstream pagemap migration
paths.

Use the BPM probe result from autotools to keep the initializer compatible on
legacy kernels while preserving the full modern initializer when available.

Signed-off-by: Varun Gupta <varun.gupta@intel.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/drm_pagemap.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_pagemap.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_pagemap.c
index b5c9c29..a8afec3 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_pagemap.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_pagemap.c
@@ -1159,7 +1159,9 @@ static int __drm_pagemap_migrate_to_ram(struct vm_area_struct *vas,
 				  MIGRATE_VMA_SELECT_DEVICE_COHERENT |
 				  MIGRATE_VMA_SELECT_COMPOUND,
 #endif
+#ifndef BPM_MIGRATE_VMA_FAULT_PAGE_NOT_PRESENT
 		.fault_page	= page,
+#endif
 	};
 	struct drm_pagemap_migrate_details mdetails = {};
 	struct drm_pagemap_zdd *zdd;
-- 
2.43.0

